# The MolScribe plugin's environment: MolScribe, which reads structures from
# pictures, for its worker (worker.py). Set up only when the plugin is added
# (docs/PLUGINS.md); its trained model is downloaded besides, by Meno
# (manifest.json, `downloads`).
#
# MolScribe from its repository at a fixed commit, pinned by the archive's
# hash: its release on PyPI, 1.1.1, is older, and starts sixteen processes
# for each picture it reads. Its own requirements pin old releases (timm,
# albumentations, OpenNMT-py) and numpy before 2.
#
# Locked for macOS and Windows (manifest.json, `systems`), with hashes, and
# with only what reading a picture loads and what that needs: OpenNMT-py's
# server and training, SmilesPE's training, and torch's GPU libraries for
# Linux are left out (--no-emit-package each; installed with --no-deps).
molscribe @ https://github.com/thomas0809/MolScribe/archive/7296a30413eb55436702011efdff78131f66d162.tar.gz
torch
numpy<2
pillow
